# Run at boot, in the background: once the network has an address (DHCP
# answers seconds after the boot; it waits 90 seconds for that), upload
# the kernel log (/devices/klog), the log klogsave kept of the boot before
# and, once, the graphics card's ROM into the private repository named
# in /system/settings/logpush; again two minutes later when the log has
# grown. Then it stays, asleep, for the person logged in: `logpush` typed
# by a user who may not read the settings (they hold a token) asks it to
# upload. Nothing waits for it. An image without those settings (the
# build's own: the settings are in no repository) uploads nothing: this
# says so once in its log (/temporary/logs/logpush.log) and ends, which
# is why it is a oneshot (one that has not ended while it is there for
# askers: `impulsectl status` says "starting").
description = upload the kernel log into its owner's private repository
exec = logpush boot
type = oneshot
restart = no
